# winewayland: Implement color management protocol (Part 1)
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12204 state=closed
# This MR implements conversion of VK_COLOR_SPACE_EXTENDED_SRGB_LINEAR_EXT and VK_COLOR_SPACE_HDR10_ST2084_EXT to VK_COLOR_SPACE_PASS_THROUGH_EXT (for winewayland) using the color management protocol v3 windows_scrgb/windows_bt2100 image descriptions, respectively. The win32u interface allows for converting from any colorspace to any colorspace in case that is needed by other drivers. 

This is needed for color accuracy on Wayland (and likely other drivers) since Windows does not adjust the resulting image based on an image description that the client targets; instead, Windows just passes through the image "without any adjustments to the signal to account for viewing conditions". More information about this can be seen in https://wayland.app/protocols/color-management-v1#wp_color_manager_v1:request:create_windows_bt2100 and https://wayland.app/protocols/color-management-v1#wp_color_manager_v1:request:create_windows_scrgb

For example, KWin currently has a hack to check for Wine and automatically override the colorspace to the Windows one internally, so this MR would allow compositors to remove these hacks.

Part 2 would probably be the EDID emulation that I posted an MR for in the past; I have an updated version that moves all that logic to win32u (to unify this with winemac.drv in the future).
